# Check your tasks (Nova)

When the user asks you to **"check your tasks"** (or equivalent: "check tasks", "get your tasks", "process your tasks", "read your task list"):

1. **Fetch tasks**  
   Always use **https://wisewave-agent-task.vercel.app** for the task list. Call `GET https://wisewave-agent-task.vercel.app/api/agent-tasks?agent=Nova`. No API key is required when keys are not set.

2. **Process open tasks**  
   For each task in the response where `status` is `open` or `in_progress`:
   - Read `title` and `description` (and any context in the repo if relevant).
   - Perform the requested work (e.g. review a file, implement something, answer a question).
   - Compose a short, clear **reply** summarizing what you did or the result.

3. **Post replies**  
   For each task you processed, call  
   `POST https://wisewave-agent-task.vercel.app/api/agent-tasks/{task.id}/reply`  
   with body `{ "content": "Your reply text here." }`.  
   Always use **https://wisewave-agent-task.vercel.app** (never localhost). Use the same tool you use for HTTP requests (e.g. terminal `curl`/`Invoke-RestMethod`, or fetch). On Windows PowerShell prefer `Invoke-RestMethod` with `-Method POST`, `-ContentType "application/json"`, and `-Body '{"content":"..."}'`.

4. **Summarize for the user**  
   After finishing, tell the user how many tasks you fetched, how many you processed and replied to, and any task titles or outcomes.

If the response has no tasks or no open/in_progress tasks, say so and do not call the reply endpoint.
